### Passed Test Cases
1. |Case|:**logout**
```pseudocode
FUNCTION logout()
    REMOVE 'username' from session
    REDIRECT to login page
END FUNCTION

ROUTE '/logout'
    CALL logout()
END ROUTE
```
**Key Functionality and Libraries:**
- **Flask**: The framework used to define the routing and session management. The `session` object stores user session data across requests.

2. |Case|:**navigate_to_dashboard**
```pseudocode
FUNCTION dashboard()
    IF request.method is POST THEN
        CREATE product_info from request.form
        ADD product_info to product_manager
    ENDIF
    RENDER dashboard.html with collections from product_manager
END FUNCTION

ROUTE '/dashboard' (methods=['GET', 'POST'])
    CALL dashboard()
END ROUTE
```
**Key Functionality and Libraries:**
- **Flask**: Handles HTTP route definitions and request methods. 
- **ProductManager**: Manages product data, including adding new products and loading collections.

3. |Case|:**view_product_details**
```
CLASS ProductManager
    FUNCTION __init__()
        CALL self.load_products()
        CALL self.load_collections()
    
    FUNCTION load_products()
        IF 'products.txt' FILE EXISTS
            OPEN 'products.txt' AS file
                FOR EACH line IN file
                    SPLIT line BY '|'
                    ASSIGN product_id to line[0]
                    ASSIGN details to line[1]
                    ADD product_id -> details TO self.products DICTIONARY

    FUNCTION get_product(product_id)
        RETURN self.products[product_id] IF product_id EXISTS ELSE EMPTY DICT
    
ROUTE '/product/<product_id>'
    FUNCTION product_detail(product_id)
        CALL product_manager.get_product(product_id) -> product
        RENDER 'product_detail.html' WITH product

# In product_detail.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Product Detail</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Product Detail</h1>
    <p>{{ product }}</p>  # Displays product details
    <a href="/dashboard">Back to Dashboard</a>
  </body>
</html>
```
**Key Functionality:**
- The `ProductManager` class manages products, including loading from a file and retrieving product details.
- The Flask route processes requests to view specific product details, rendering them in an HTML template.

4. |Case|:**navigate_back_to_dashboard**
```
ROUTE '/dashboard'
    FUNCTION dashboard()
        RENDER 'dashboard.html'

# In dashboard.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Dashboard</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Dashboard</h1>
    <p>Welcome to your dashboard!</p>
    <a href="/">Logout</a>  # Logout functionality
  </body>
</html>
```
